# [Add Strings](https://leetcode.com/problems/add-strings/)

## Approach: Digit-by-Digit Addition

### Intuition
- Traverse both strings from right to left, starting with the least significant digits.
- Add the corresponding digits along with the carry (`rem`).
- Store the last digit of the sum using `sum % 10` and update the carry using `sum / 10`.
- If one string has remaining digits, add them along with the carry.
- Append the final carry if it exists.
- Reverse the result string to obtain the correct answer.

### Code
```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    string addStrings(string num1, string num2) {
        int i1 = num1.length() - 1, i2 = num2.length() - 1;
        string res = "";
        int rem = 0;

        while (i1 >= 0 && i2 >= 0) {
            int n1 = num1[i1] - '0';
            int n2 = num2[i2] - '0';

            int sum = n1 + n2 + rem;
            rem = sum / 10;

            res += to_string(sum % 10);

            i1--;
            i2--;
        }

        while (i1 >= 0) {
            int sum = (num1[i1] - '0') + rem;
            rem = sum / 10;

            res += to_string(sum % 10);
            i1--;
        }

        while (i2 >= 0) {
            int sum = (num2[i2] - '0') + rem;
            rem = sum / 10;

            res += to_string(sum % 10);
            i2--;
        }

        if (rem) res += to_string(rem);

        reverse(res.begin(), res.end());
        return res;
    }
};
```

### Complexity Analysis
- **Time Complexity:** \(O(\max(n,m))\), where \(n\) and \(m\) are the lengths of the two strings.
- **Space Complexity:** \(O(\max(n,m))\) for storing the result.

### Key Takeaway
String-based addition allows us to add arbitrarily large non-negative integers without converting them into built-in numeric types. The carry mechanism is the same as in elementary addition.
